<title>FRANCE: New York top destination for Paris 1996 cargo exports.</title>
<headline>New York top destination for Paris 1996 cargo exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in 1996, despite a strong decline in traffic on 1995 levels.</p>
<p>The top ten destinations for ADP exports in 1996 and the percentage change on 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p>			   1996 Exports   Percent change from 1995</p>
<p>  1.  New York	     38,939     down   16.5</p>
<p>  2.  Chicago	     27,780	 up   14.6</p>
<p>  3.  Tokyo		 26,355     down   10.8</p>
<p>  4.  Hong Kong	   24,700	 up    2.5</p>
<p>  5.  Mexico City	 12,382     down   33.1</p>
<p>  6.  Sao Paulo	   12,158     down    7.3</p>
<p>  7   Montreal	    12,058     down   17.9</p>
<p>  8.  Los Angeles	 11,928	 up    2.8</p>
<p>  9.  Dubai		  9,310     down    3.9</p>
<p> 10.  Miami		  9,233	 up   90.2</p>
<p>-- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
